1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,020
Joseph Borrell, the EU foreign policy chief, said that he expects EU leaders to work toward a call for a humanitarian pause in what's happening in Gaza to bring in some aid.

2
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:14,660
Is the United States in conversations with the Europeans about that? Would the United States support such a call?

3
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:19,340
We are in conversations with the Europeans about this question of getting humanitarian aid in,

4
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:25,780
and we are in conversations with the government of Israel and the government of Egypt about how best to get humanitarian aid in.

5
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:29,840
But I think with this question, whether you call it a pause or whether you call it a ceasefire,

6
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:39,220
you have to think about what that would mean in this context when Israel has suffered this terrorist attack and Israel continues to suffer ongoing terrorist attacks.

7
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:44,380
There are rockets, as I said a moment ago, that continue to be launched from Gaza targeting Israel.

8
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:52,640
Any ceasefire would give Hamas the ability to rest, to refit, and to get ready to continue launching terrorist attacks against Israel.

9
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:58,260
You can understand perfectly clearly why that's an intolerable situation for Israel,

10
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:03,260
as it would be an intolerable situation for any country that has suffered such a brutal terrorist attack

11
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:07,240
and continues to see the terrorist threat right on its borders.

12
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:15,360
So what we will continue to do with respect to this question is focus on getting humanitarian assistance in to Gaza.

13
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:20,580
We've seen deliveries go in for the past three days, and our special envoy on the ground, David Satterfield,

14
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:26,180
is working intensively to establish ongoing mechanisms for the delivery of humanitarian assistance,

15
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,740
and we're working to establish places where civilians can be safe from harm.

16
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:30,100
Thank you.

17
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:30,160
Thank you.

18
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:30,180
Thank you.

